<section>
  <p><em>Last updated: October 4, 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    This policy covers Tempo Adjust for Safari, Bandcamp Tempo Adjust, and
    Discogs Tempo Adjust (together, "Tempo Adjust").
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Personally-Identifying Information</h2>
  <p>
    Tempo Adjust does not collect or transmit any Personally-Identifying
    Information. It also does not collect anonymized or aggregate information
    such as usage statistics, device type, or crash reports. Tempo Adjust
    contains no analytics or tracking code.
  </p>

  <p>
    Your settings, detected BPMs, and cached exchange rates are stored only on
    your device, in the extension's local storage. They are never sent to the
    developer or to anyone else, and they are removed when you uninstall the
    extension.
  </p>

  <p>
    To do its job, Tempo Adjust makes two kinds of network requests from your
    browser:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>BPM detection</strong> downloads the audio of the track you are
      listening to from Bandcamp's own servers, the same way the page's player
      does, and analyzes it on your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Purchase export</strong> fetches currency exchange rates from
      <a href="https://frankfurter.dev">frankfurter.dev</a>, a free, open-source
      service. That request contains only dates and currency codes. Your
      purchases and account details stay in your browser.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Tips in the Safari app are handled entirely by Apple through in-app
    purchase. Tempo Adjust never sees your payment details. Apple's handling of
    that transaction is covered by
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Business Transfers</h2>
  <p>
    If Tempo Adjust, or substantially all of its assets, were acquired, or in
    the unlikely event that its developer goes out of business or enters
    bankruptcy, this policy and its effects may change or be amended. Since
    Tempo Adjust holds no user data, there would be no user data to transfer.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Privacy Policy Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy may change from time to time, at the developer's sole
    discretion. Your continued use of Tempo Adjust after any changes to this
    Privacy Policy will constitute your acceptance of those changes.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
